<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">14</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-colline-gate"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-colline-gate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Colline Gate</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 82 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Colline Gate was fought on 1 November 82 BCE outside the walls of Rome.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lauron"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Lauron</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 76 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Lauron was fought in 76 BCE in eastern Spain during the Sertorian War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cabira"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Cabira</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 72 or 71 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Cabira was fought near Cabira in Pontus, in the Third Mithridatic War, in 72 or 71 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-sabis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-sabis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Sabis</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 57 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Sabis was fought in 57 BCE on the river Sabis, usually identified with the Sambre, in northern Gaul.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alesia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-alesia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Alesia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · Siege · 52 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Alesia was the decisive siege of the Gallic Wars, fought in 52 BCE at the hill-fort of the Mandubii, probably at Alise-Sainte-Reine in Burgundy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ilerda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-ilerda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ilerda</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 49 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ilerda was Julius Caesar's campaign of June to August 49 BCE near modern Lleida in north-eastern Spain against the Pompeian legates Afranius and Petreius…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-bagradas-river-49-bce"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Bagradas River (49 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 49 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Bagradas River was fought in August 49 BCE in the province of Africa, near the river now called the Medjerda in Tunisia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pharsalus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-pharsalus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Pharsalus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 48 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Pharsalus was fought on 9 August 48 BCE near Pharsalus in Thessaly between Julius Caesar and the larger army of Pompey and the Senate.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-thapsus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-thapsus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Thapsus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 46 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Thapsus was fought on 6 April 46 BCE near Thapsus, on the coast of present-day Tunisia, between Julius Caesar and the Pompeian forces of Metellus Scipio…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-munda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-munda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Munda</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 45 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Munda was fought on 17 March 45 BCE in southern Spain between Julius Caesar and the Pompeian army of Gnaeus and Sextus Pompeius and Titus Labienus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-philippi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-philippi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Philippi</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 42 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Philippi was fought in October 42 BCE near the city of Philippi in eastern Macedonia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-actium"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-actium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Actium</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 31 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Actium was a naval battle fought in 31 BCE off western Greece between Octavian and the combined forces of Mark Antony and Cleopatra VII.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/clades-lolliana"><span class="enc-name">Clades Lolliana</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 16 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The clades Lolliana was a Roman defeat in 16 BCE, when the Sugambri, Usipetes and Tencteri crossed the Rhine and routed the legate Marcus Lollius, capturing the eagle…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-sagra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-sagra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Sagra</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 6th century BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Sagra was fought in the 6th century BCE beside the river Sagras in Calabria, where the small army of Locri Epizephyrii defeated a much larger force…</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-uxellodunum"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Uxellodunum</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 51 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The siege of Uxellodunum in 51 BCE was the last major operation of Julius Caesar's conquest of Gaul.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/perusine-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/perusine-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Perusine War</span><span class="enc-type">War · Siege · 41–40 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Perusine War was a Roman civil conflict of 41–40 BCE between Octavian and the consul Lucius Antonius, backed by Fulvia, wife of Mark Antony.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">20</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/social-war-91-87-bce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Social War (91–87 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">War · Revolt · 91–87 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Social War was the revolt of Rome's Italian allies, led by the Marsi and Samnites, who demanded Roman citizenship.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-mithridatic-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/first-mithridatic-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">First Mithridatic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 89–85 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The First Mithridatic War was fought from 89 to 85 BCE between Rome and Mithridates VI of Pontus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mithridatic-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mithridatic-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mithridatic Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 89–63 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mithridatic Wars were three wars fought between the Roman Republic and Mithridates VI of Pontus from 89 to 63 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-mithridatic-war"><span class="enc-name">Second Mithridatic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 83–81 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Second Mithridatic War (83–81 BCE) was a short conflict between Rome and Mithridates VI of Pontus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sullas-civil-war"><span class="enc-name">Sulla's civil war</span><span class="enc-type">War · 83–82 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">Sulla's civil war was fought in 83–82 BCE between Lucius Cornelius Sulla, returning from the war against Mithridates, and the Marian faction governing Rome.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sertorian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sertorian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sertorian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 80–72 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sertorian War was a Roman civil war fought in Hispania from 80 to 72 BCE between Quintus Sertorius, a supporter of the Marian party, and the government in Rome…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/third-mithridatic-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/third-mithridatic-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Third Mithridatic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 73–63 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Third Mithridatic War of 73–63 BCE was the last war between Rome and Mithridates VI of Pontus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gallic-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gallic-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gallic Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 58–50 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Gallic Wars were the campaigns of Julius Caesar in Gaul from 58 to 50 BCE, which brought the whole of Gaul west of the Rhine under Roman rule.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-civil-war"><span class="enc-name">Xiongnu civil war</span><span class="enc-type">War · 57 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Xiongnu civil war was a succession conflict among rival claimants to the position of chanyu that split the Xiongnu Empire around 57 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-parthian-wars"><span class="enc-name">Roman–Parthian Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 54 BCE – 217 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Roman–Parthian Wars were the conflicts between Rome and the Parthian Empire from 54 BCE to 217 CE, the first phase of the Roman–Persian Wars.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-persian-wars"><span class="enc-name">Roman–Persian Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 54 BCE – 628 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Roman–Persian Wars were a long series of conflicts between the Roman (later Byzantine) state and the Parthian and then Sasanian empires of Iran, lasting from 54 BCE…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/caesars-civil-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Caesar's Civil War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 49–45 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">Caesar's Civil War was fought from 49 to 45 BCE between Julius Caesar and the conservative faction of the Roman Senate led by Pompey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/liberators-civil-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/liberators-civil-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Liberators' civil war</span><span class="enc-type">War · 44–42 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Liberators' civil war was the Roman civil war that followed the assassination of Julius Caesar in 44 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/octavians-illyrian-campaign"><span class="enc-name">Octavian's Illyrian campaign</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 35–33 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">Octavian's Illyrian campaign of 35–33 BCE was a series of Roman operations led by the future Augustus along the eastern Adriatic and in its hinterland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/final-war-of-the-roman-republic"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/final-war-of-the-roman-republic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Final War of the Roman Republic</span><span class="enc-type">War · 32–30 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Final War of the Roman Republic was the civil war of 32–30 BCE between Octavian and the alliance of Mark Antony and Cleopatra VII of Egypt.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-annexation-of-egypt"><span class="enc-name">Roman annexation of Egypt</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 30 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Roman annexation of Egypt took place in 30 BCE, when Octavian took Alexandria after the defeat of Mark Antony and Cleopatra VII.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cantabrian-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cantabrian Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 29–19 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cantabrian Wars were Rome's final conquest of the Iberian Peninsula, fought from 29 to 19 BCE against the Cantabri and Astures of the northern mountains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-expedition-against-the-garamantes-19-bce"><span class="enc-name">Roman expedition against the Garamantes (19 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 19 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Roman expedition against the Garamantes was a punitive campaign led in 19 BCE by Lucius Cornelius Balbus, the proconsul of Africa, into the Fezzan region of the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lelantine-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lelantine-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lelantine War</span><span class="enc-type">War · late 8th–7th century BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Lelantine War was a conflict between the Euboean cities of Chalcis and Eretria over the fertile Lelantine plain that lay between them, fought around the late 8th or…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-messenian-war"><span class="enc-name">Second Messenian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · Revolt · 7th century BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Second Messenian War was a revolt of the Messenians against Spartan rule in the seventh century BCE, traditionally led by the hero Aristomenes.</span></a></li></ul></section>
